---
/*
 * Privacy (conversion spec 3.6): one screen that says what the form stores
 * and how to remove it. Plain text on Paper, no CTA, no tracking events.
 * The owner reviews the wording (conversion spec open item 5).
 */
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site.config';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="What Digitally Shifted stores when you send an enquiry, why we store it, and how to have it removed."
  path="/privacy"
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  noindex={true}
>
  <h2>What we store</h2>
  <p>
    When you send us an enquiry through our forms, we store the details you
    send: your name, email address or phone number, your business name when
    you give it, and your message, with the date.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we store it</h2>
  <p>To reply to your enquiry and to prepare any quote you asked for.</p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your details. We do not pass them to third parties for
    their own marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>How to have your details removed</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and ask us to
    remove your details. We will delete them and confirm that we have done it.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
